MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d3139b830089d814fbd239d3511709d3, type: 3}
  m_Name: StartingGameDialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Messages:
  - message: "There was a small quaint village deep in the woods. The area they called
      home wasn\u2019t the most suitable for life."
    wordsToBold: []
  - message: "Nature was hardly kind to these villagers. They\u2019d have to walk
      long distances for water, and foraging for food proved even more difficult.
      Still, they managed."
    wordsToBold: []
  - message: 'They had no other choice except to live here, for a miasmic fog was
      plaguing the land and cornered all inhabitants here. '
    wordsToBold: []
  - message: "Fear had taken hold of everyone\u2019s minds and made the people afraid
      of each other. Order collapsed as panic set in. The civilization had split
      off and began living far away from each other, creating smaller villages instead."
    wordsToBold: []
  - message: 'No one could explain where the fog came from or how it manifested,
      but it spread throughout the area, killing people, wildlife and rotting plant
      life. '
    wordsToBold: []
  - message: 'Faced with death, the people had turned to their faith. Their faith
      was in the Moon Goddess as she shone down through the night sky before the
      fog shrouded it in a thick purple blanket. '
    wordsToBold: []
  - message: People knew that Moonlight could repel the fog. Her light was their
      protection, and everyone had built a Moon Statue of their own to fight off
      the miasma.
    wordsToBold: []
  - message: "Still, prayers couldn\u2019t save the people, and it\u2019s assumed
      that nearly half of the people had died from the fog. Prayers couldn\u2019t
      save your village either. "
    wordsToBold: []
  - message: "Now, you\u2019re the only one left of your village. Desperation clings
      to your soul as you refuse to make peace in death. While you can\u2019t bring
      them back, you have a fighting chance to combat the silent death\u2026"
    wordsToBold: []
